  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:6320",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the inhibition of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-6 through a multi-step mechanism involving the target A704 and 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a modulator of the metabolic pathway leading to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-6, with A704 serving as a critical intermediate in this process. This pathway is further supported by the presence of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which directly targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-6. The integration of these targets indicates a potential role for Mollicellin N in modulating the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-6, likely through the regulation of the downstream metabolite 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link between Mollicellin N and UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-6, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores suggest a plausible relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance.",
